---
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout title="About me"><div class="shell index-page"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE GARDEN</span><h1>Hello, I’m windyx3<span class="heading-dot">.</span></h1><p>A personal space for learning, coding, recording, and sharing.</p></header><div class="prose"><h2>Why this space exists</h2><p>This website is a home for learning notes, programming knowledge, projects, and personal reflections, along with tools, books, and websites worth keeping.</p><p>I want these pieces to accumulate into a digital garden I can revisit, connect, and keep tending.</p><blockquote><p>Stay curious. Keep a record.Give ideas a place to grow.</p></blockquote><h2>What you will find here</h2><ul><li><a href={withBase('/notes/')}>Notes / Wiki</a>: knowledge and algorithm notes organized by topic.</li><li><a href={withBase('/blog/')}>Blog</a>: technical writing, personal reflections, and everyday discoveries.</li><li><a href={withBase('/projects/')}>Projects</a>: the journey from an idea to something that works.</li><li><a href={withBase('/interests/')}>Favorites</a>: interests and resources worth keeping.</li></ul><h2>Find me elsewhere</h2><p><a href={site.github}>GitHub / windyx3 ↗</a> · <a href={withBase('/rss.xml')}>Subscribe via RSS ↗</a></p><hr /><p class="muted">This garden is just getting started. The initial sample notes and favorites illustrate its structure and can gradually be replaced with personal content.</p></div></div></BaseLayout>
